<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="whr-customization-image">
  <title>How to Change Image Styles</title>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm product="webhelp-responsive">WebHelp Responsive<indexterm>Images<indexterm>outputclass</indexterm></indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <keywords>
        <keyword outputclass="label" product="webhelp-responsive">CSS Styling</keyword>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_intro">In WebHelp Responsive output, you can adapt the background of an image to the
      selected theme by using the <xmlatt>outputclass="backdrop"</xmlatt> attribute. When this value
      is used, the image background is transparent in light mode and white in dark
      mode:<codeblock outputclass="language-xml" id="codeblock_example">&lt;image href="../img/sample.png" outputclass="backdrop"/></codeblock></p>
    <p>You can control these colors using the <codeph>--wh-image-bg</codeph> CSS property:</p>
    <codeblock id="codeblock_c1k_mml_pkc" outputclass="language-css">:root {
  ...
  --wh-image-bg: lightgray;
}

@media screen {
  :root[data-wh-theme="dark"] {
    color-scheme: dark;
    ...
    --wh-image-bg: lightgray;
  }
}</codeblock>
    <note id="note_tjl_2nl_pkc">This is supported for both <xmlelement>image</xmlelement> and
        <xmlelement>imagemap</xmlelement> elements.</note>
  </body>
</topic>
